        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Towel/Napkin Borders which have been cut, joined together and attached to new fabric.  Linen embroidered with silk in double darning and musabak stitch, and metal thread in a diagonal filling stitch and with plate in satin stitch.\nThere is a narrow border above the main one; it is a densely packed  floral meander with a metal thread stem, small pink or blue flowers and small pointed leaves. The main border is decorated with a series of large arches supported by columns, all worked in metal thread.  Within each arch are four small cypress trees between pairs of larger cypress trees; these are alternately dark or light green. Above the trees is a two-storey domed building, predominantly pink and silver, with silver palm-tree leaves around the roof.\nThe embroidery has been cut and hemmed along both sides."@en ;
